Ah.  I thought you meant "unlimited resources other than pudding farming", 
not "unlimited resources other than producing and killing monsters".  
(FYI, summon nasties doesn't respect extinction either)

Although "normal" extinctionist farming does have an eventual limit , it 
is still excessively powerful, given the low amount of skill needed and 
the large gains it produces.

Consider a wizard (magic res) who descends to Sokoban (reflection, a good 
starting supply of food), then goes to Minetown (picking up some good 
armor on the way), then heads back to DL1 with whatever useful items he's 
found or bought.  there's an altar on level 1, which is nice, but hardly 
extreme good luck.  He digs out the level and spends a few hundred 
thousand turns killing and sacrificing the randomly generated monsters.  
He prays for boons, spellbooks, and occasionally food (monsters will 
sometimes drop food rations, and as he gains levels high-nutrition 
monsters will start showing up).  Eventually he has enough golden glows 
and death-drop items to proceed safely [1] through the rest of the game 

Although some ability is required to execute this strategy (a severely 
retarded person would be unable to), it is essentially a test of the 
player's willingness to waste dozens of hours of real life time [2] in 
what is essentially computerized masturbation.  It is not a test of 
Nethack skill.




[1] Yes, "safe" in nethack is always relative.
